Claude Design skill for openclaude
==================================

This bundled skill ships content adapted from several upstream sources:

1. The Claude Design master system prompt — released by Anthropic Labs
   on 2026-04-17 with the Claude Design product (claude.ai/design).
   Adapted to remove proprietary tool references and rewire the
   workflow onto Claude Code's native tools.

2. Open Design (https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design) — an Apache-2.0
   open-source replica of Claude Design. We vendor:

   - The skills/<name>/SKILL.md prompt bodies as references/skills/*.md
     (111 named workflows: frontend-design, web-artifacts-builder,
     login-flow, resume-modern, data-report, poster-hero,
     brand-guidelines, the deck-* / slides / ppt-keynote family,
     remotion, threejs, shader-dev, d3-visualization, shadcn-ui, the
     gsap-* and frame-* families, figma-*, and many more). External
     paid-API generative-media skills (fal-*, venice-*, replicate,
     minimax-*, imagen, imagegen, sora, speech, pixelbin-media,
     nanobanana-ppt, gif-sticker-maker, ai-music-album) are excluded.

   - The craft/*.md design-discipline guidelines as references/craft/*.md
     (12 docs: anti-ai-slop, accessibility-baseline, animation-discipline,
     color, form-validation, laws-of-ux, rtl-and-bidi, state-coverage,
     typography-hierarchy, typography-hierarchy-editorial, typography).

   - A representative subset of design-systems/<name>/DESIGN.md files
     as references/design-systems/*.md (27 brand systems).

   - The design-templates/html-ppt/assets/themes/*.css theme overrides,
     design-templates/html-ppt/templates/single-page/*.html slide
     templates, and design-templates/html-ppt/references/*.md authoring
     docs as references/html-ppt/themes|templates|refs/*, plus
     design-templates/html-ppt/assets/runtime.js.

3. design.md (https://github.com/google-labs-code/design.md) — Apache-2.0.
   We vendor docs/spec.md and the canonical examples/ (atmospheric-glass,
   paws-and-paths, totality-festival) as references/design-md/, plus a
   hand-authored cli.md cheat-sheet for the `npx @google/design.md` CLI.

4. gameuidatabase skill (coffeegrind123/claude-sbox-setup ecosystem) —
   integrated in full as references/game-ui/ for building and mocking
   game UIs. Drives gameuidatabase.com (Edd Coates' archive); the site
   itself is third-party and not redistributed here.

5. taste-skill (https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill) — an MIT-licensed
   (© 2026 Leonxlnx) anti-slop frontend framework. We adapt (not verbatim
   vendor — rewritten to this skill's HTML-artifact workflow and house
   style) an anti-slop TASTE LAYER. These files are skill-local, NOT
   produced by scripts/vendor.ts from Open Design; the script snapshots
   them before its wipe and restores them after, and folds the recipes
   into the generated references/skills/_INDEX.md:

   - references/craft/taste-dials.md — the Design Read (brief inference),
     the three dials (DESIGN_VARIANCE / MOTION_INTENSITY / VISUAL_DENSITY),
     and anti-default discipline (taste-skill SKILL.md §0, §1, §7).
   - references/craft/redesign-audit.md — audit-first redesign protocol +
     concrete fix catalog (taste-skill redesign skill + §11).
   - references/craft/output-completeness.md — anti-truncation enforcement
     + its laziness-research basis (taste-skill full-output-enforcement).
   - references/craft/anti-ai-slop-taste.md — the extended slop-tell
     catalog and the em-dash ban (taste-skill §4, §9).
   - references/skills/image-to-code.md and imagegen-frontend.md — concise
     image-direction recipes (from taste-skill image-to-code and
     imagegen-frontend-web|mobile).

   Note: upstream Open Design now vendors the FULL taste-skill collection
   itself (taste-skill, brandkit, minimalist-skill, brutalist-skill,
   soft-skill, redesign-skill, output-skill, image-to-code-skill,
   imagegen-frontend-web|mobile, stitch-skill, and more). We therefore do
   NOT keep local copies of taste-skill.md or brandkit.md — the fuller
   upstream versions flow through unchanged. The skill-local recipes above
   are distinct, differently-named concise variants; imagegen-frontend.md
   is also distinct from the Open Design skill named "imagegen", which is
   excluded from the upstream vendor (see the exclusion set in vendor.ts).

